Step 1: Create the static folders

Run this in your project folder (the one with app.py), while you're online:

mkdir -p static/js static/css

Step 2: Download the libraries

curl -L -o static/js/marked.min.js https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked/marked.min.js
curl -L -o static/js/highlight.min.js https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/highlight.js/11.9.0/highlight.min.js
curl -L -o static/css/github-dark.min.css https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/highlight.js/11.9.0/styles/github-dark.min.css

On Windows, if curl isn't available, open each URL in your browser and use Save As into those folders.
Step 3: Find the CDN tags in your HTML

Open templates/index.html and search for cdn, jsdelivr, cdnjs, or unpkg. Note every external <script src="https://..."> and <link href="https://...">.
Step 4: Replace them with local paths

<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ url_for('static', filename='css/github-dark.min.css') }}">
<script src="{{ url_for('static', filename='js/marked.min.js') }}"></script>
<script src="{{ url_for('static', filename='js/highlight.min.js') }}"></script>

Keep the order: marked and highlight must load before your own app.js.
Step 5: Move your own JS and CSS into static (if needed)

Your repo has app.js and style.css in the root folder. Flask only serves files from static/, so if index.html references them, move them and update the tags:

mv app.js static/js/app.js
mv style.css static/css/style.css

<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ url_for('static', filename='css/style.css') }}">
<script src="{{ url_for('static', filename='js/app.js') }}"></script>

If they already load fine, leave them alone.
Step 6: Check for other CDN assets

Fonts (Google Fonts), icons (Font Awesome), or a copy-button library may also load from the internet. Download them the same way, or the layout will still break offline.
Step 7: Test offline

    Restart the app with python app.py.
    Turn off your internet (keep LM Studio running).
    Hard refresh the page with Ctrl + Shift + R.
    Ask for code, for example "Write a Python binary search."
    Press F12 and open the Network tab. Everything should load from 127.0.0.1:5000 with no red failed requests.

